{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["Take heed, regarding the plague of leprosy, to take great heed and to do — that even if he is a king like Uzziah, they must not show him deference, but he must be confined the seven days and they must send him away and he must dwell alone." "According to all that they instruct you — as it says: זכור את אשר עשה יקוק אלהיך למרים — that even though she was a prophetess and the sister of Moshe, they showed her no deference, but she was confined seven days."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:39:26.548182717Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}